---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Icon from "../../components/Icon.astro";
import { absoluteUrl, AUTHOR, DOCS_DESCRIPTION } from "../../data/site";
const rootBase = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const root = rootBase.endsWith("/") ? rootBase : rootBase + "/";
const jsExample = [
  'import { createChecker } from "italian-profanity";',
  "",
  "const checker = createChecker({",
  '  profile: "balanced",',
  '  languages: ["it"],',
  "  contacts: false,",
  "  maxLength: 64,",
  "});",
  "",
  'const result = checker.check("D10 p0rc0");',
  'if (result.action === "block") {',
  "  // Reject the submitted nickname.",
  "}",
].join("\n");
const dartExample = [
  "import 'package:italian_profanity/italian_profanity.dart';",
  "",
  "final checker = ItalianProfanity.createChecker(",
  "  profile: Profile.balanced,",
  "  languages: ['it'],",
  "  contacts: false,",
  "  maxLength: 64,",
  ");",
  "",
  "final result = checker.check('Claudio');",
  "if (result.action == Action.block) {",
  "  // Reject the submitted nickname.",
  "}",
].join("\n");
const docsUrl = absoluteUrl("docs/");
const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@type": "TechArticle",
    headline: "italian-profanity developer documentation",
    description: DOCS_DESCRIPTION,
    url: docsUrl,
    inLanguage: "en",
    author: AUTHOR,
    about: { "@id": `${absoluteUrl()}#software` },
    proficiencyLevel: "Beginner",
  },
  {
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: absoluteUrl() },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Documentation", item: docsUrl },
    ],
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Docs: Italian Profanity Filter for JS, TypeScript & Flutter — italian-profanity" description={DOCS_DESCRIPTION} canonicalPath="docs/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="docs-hero">
      <div class="shell"><a class="docs-back" href={root}>← Back to home</a>
        <h1>LESS GUESSWORK.<br /><em>MORE CONTROL.</em></h1>
        <p>Install the filter, pick a policy and validate user input without an API or external service.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="docs-layout shell">
      <aside class="docs-sidebar">
        <nav aria-label="Documentation sections">
          <strong>ON THIS PAGE</strong>
          <a href="#quickstart">01 / Quick start</a>
          <a href="#api">02 / API</a>
          <a href="#policy">03 / Policies</a>
          <a href="#customization">04 / Customization</a>
          <a href="#production">05 / Production notes</a>
          <a href="#limits">06 / Limitations</a>
        </nav>
        <a class="docs-sidebar-external" href="https://github.com/eliazv/italian-profanity/blob/master/docs/integrazione.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Full integration guide ↗</a>
      </aside>
      <article class="docs-content">
        <section id="quickstart" class="docs-section">
          <span class="docs-n">01</span><h2>Quick start</h2>
          <p>Use the JavaScript package in Node or browsers, or the pure Dart package in Flutter. Both share their detection rules and expected results.</p>
          <div class="docs-code-title">JAVASCRIPT / TYPESCRIPT <button type="button" data-copy="npm install italian-profanity">COPY COMMAND</button></div>
          <pre><code>npm install italian-profanity</code></pre>
          <pre><code>{jsExample}</code></pre>
          <div class="docs-code-title">DART / FLUTTER <button type="button" data-copy="flutter pub add italian_profanity">COPY COMMAND</button></div>
          <pre><code>flutter pub add italian_profanity</code></pre>
          <pre><code>{dartExample}</code></pre>
          <p>For Dart packages outside Flutter, run <code>dart pub add italian_profanity</code>.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="api" class="docs-section">
          <span class="docs-n">02</span><h2>API</h2>
          <p>Four entry points are shared between TypeScript and Dart:</p>
          <div class="docs-table-wrap"><table class="docs-table"><thead><tr><th>Function</th><th>Use it for</th></tr></thead><tbody>
            <tr><td><code>check(text)</code></td><td>Get an action (<code>allow</code>, <code>review</code> or <code>block</code>) and the matches.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>findMatches(text)</code></td><td>Inspect detected rules without applying a moderation decision.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>isClean(text)</code></td><td>Return true only when the action is <code>allow</code>, not <code>review</code>.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>createChecker(options)</code></td><td>Reuse the same policy, languages, exceptions and settings across checks.</td></tr>
          </tbody></table></div>
          <p>A match describes its category, severity, confidence and location in the original string. Locations are UTF-16 offsets; treat them as potentially sensitive.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="policy" class="docs-section">
          <span class="docs-n">03</span><h2>Policies</h2>
          <div class="policy-grid">
            <div><strong>Balanced</strong><p>The default, designed to reduce false positives on common names.</p></div>
            <div><strong>Strict</strong><p>More restrictive with ambiguous wording. Review its impact before deployment.</p></div>
            <div><strong>Lenient</strong><p>Less restrictive for products where warnings may be more useful than rejection.</p></div>
          </div>
          <p>Make your product policy explicit. If you have no manual review queue, you might reject only <code>block</code> and handle <code>review</code> separately. Do not assume <code>isClean()</code> makes that distinction for you.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="customization" class="docs-section">
          <span class="docs-n">04</span><h2>Customization</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Languages:</strong> Italian is on by default. Enable curated English coverage with <code>languages: ["it", "en"]</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Contacts:</strong> Optional detection for URL, email and phone-like text via <code>contacts: true</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Extra rules:</strong> Add product-specific whole-word rules rather than changing the shared dataset.</li>
            <li><strong>Exceptions and thresholds:</strong> Tune category sensitivity without rewriting the detector.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>The full integration guide covers the option contracts and migration from existing filters.</p>
          <a class="docs-inline-link" href="https://github.com/eliazv/italian-profanity/blob/master/docs/integrazione.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open integration guide ↗</a>
        </section>
        <section id="production" class="docs-section">
          <span class="docs-n">05</span><h2>Production notes</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Recheck on your server.</strong> Client-side checks improve UX but can always be bypassed.</li>
            <li><strong>Keep versions aligned.</strong> Share the same release and options across backend and mobile clients.</li>
            <li><strong>Validate input length separately.</strong> A filter may inspect only the configured prefix of long text.</li>
            <li><strong>Protect privacy.</strong> Avoid saving actual nicknames, matches or offsets in moderation telemetry.</li>
            <li><strong>Review release behavior diffs.</strong> New rules may change decisions for previously allowed input.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section id="limits" class="docs-section">
          <span class="docs-n">06</span><h2>Limitations</h2>
          <div class="docs-warning"><strong>A lexical filter is not full moderation.</strong><p>The library does not understand intent or context and cannot guarantee that an allowed input is appropriate. Some ambiguous names deliberately produce <code>review</code>.</p></div>
          <p>Regional dialects are only partially covered. The optional English dataset is curated, but is not equivalent to a complete English-language moderation service. Evaluate the library on real use cases before enforcing strict blocking.</p>
          <div class="docs-final">
            <h3>See something missing?</h3><p>Reproducible examples and carefully reviewed exceptions help the project improve.</p>
            <a class="button button-dark" href="https://github.com/eliazv/italian-profanity/issues" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><Icon name="github" /> Open an issue</a>
          </div>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <script>import "../../scripts/playground.ts";</script>
</BaseLayout>
